      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Preheat oven to 160C (140C fan)."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat oil in a large casserole over high heat. Season lamb and brown in batches, 3 to 4 minutes per batch. Remove and set aside."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Reduce heat to medium. Cook onions in the same pot for 15 minutes, stirring regularly, until golden. Add garlic and ginger, cook 2 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add all spices and stir for 1 minute. Return lamb to the pot. Add honey, saffron water and 400ml water. Stir to combine."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Cover and transfer to the oven. Cook for 1 hour 30 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Remove from oven. Add prunes (or dates). Return to oven uncovered for 30 minutes until the sauce thickens and the fruit is soft."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Scatter with toasted almonds and coriander. Serve with couscous or flatbread."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Sauce is too thin",
              "cause": "Too much water or oven temperature too low",
              "fix": "Remove the lid and return to oven for 20 minutes to reduce. The sauce should coat the back of a spoon."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Lamb still chewy after 2 hours",
              "cause": "Shoulder cut with more connective tissue than average",
              "fix": "Cover and return to oven for a further 30 minutes. Lamb shoulder becomes tender eventually; it will not remain tough."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The lamb and fruit tagine is most associated with the imperial cities of Morocco: Fez, Marrakech and Meknes. It is a dish of celebration, served at weddings and Eid. The sweet-savoury combination reflects the influence of Andalusian cooking brought to Morocco by Moorish exiles from Spain in the 15th century. Apricot and quince versions follow the same structure as this prune variation."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
